==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈvɛr̥pa/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɛr̥pa|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|is|non|verpa}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*werpaną}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-strong|varp|urpu|orpið}} ''or''<br />{{is-verb-weak|verpti|verpt}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|with dative}} to [[throw]]
# {{lb|is|ambitransitive|with dative}} to [[lay]] (an egg)
#: {{ux|is|Hænan '''verpti''' eggi.|The chicken [[lay an egg|'''laid''' an egg]].}}

=====Usage notes=====
The strong conjugation is the original one, but the weak one is becoming more usual. They are also commonly mixed together.

=====Conjugation=====
Strong conjugation:
{{is-conj-s3|v|e|rp|mp=-}}

Weak conjugation:
{{is-conj-w2|v|e|rp|mp=-}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|throw}} {{l|is|varpa}}, {{l|is|fleygja}}, {{l|is|henda}}, {{l|is|kasta}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|verpa öndinni léttar}} (to heave a sigh of relief)

===Etymology 2===
Causative of ''verpa'' (1). From {{der|is|gem-pro|*warpijaną}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|verpti|verpt}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|with accusative}} to [[twist]], [[wind]], [[contort]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj-w2|v|e|rp}}

==Latin==
{{wikipedia|Latin profanity#Mentula and verpa: the penis|''Verpa''- Latin profanity}}

===Etymology===
Possibly borrowed from a {{bor|la|gem|-}} language, related to {{der|la|gem-pro|*werpaną|t=to throw}}. More likely from {{inh|la|itc-pro|-}} source for “to turn round, to roll” (as in 'unfurl, peel back, or retract foreskin') via {{der|la|ine-pro|*welw-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*wel-||to turn, wind, round}}.

===Pronunciation===
